Title: MW–M31 Merger Kinematic Profiles Pipeline

Summary:
Completed development of a full kinematic analysis pipeline for MW–M31 merger simulation snapshots. The pipeline processes N-body data to compute radial and time-evolving kinematic profiles, including velocity dispersions (σ_r, σ_t), rotational velocity (v_rot), specific angular momentum (j), enclosed mass (M_enc), escape velocity (v_esc), and velocity anisotropy (β).

Work Completed:
- Implemented snapshot extraction system from tar archives into temporary workspace.
- Built robust center-of-mass (COM) position and velocity calculations with fallback handling.
- Developed full kinematic profile computation engine in COM frame.
- Implemented radial binning with mass-weighted statistics and noise filtering.
- Computed global kinematic scalars per snapshot for time-series diagnostics.
- Designed and generated multiple publication-quality plots:
  • Inner-halo kinematic evolution
  • (r, t) heatmaps for σ_r and β
  • Radial profile grids across merger stages
  • Angular momentum evolution
  • Escape velocity profiles
  • β anisotropy profiles
- Added detailed documentation and physical explanations throughout the code.
- Structured pipeline for scalability and HPC/batch execution.

Notes:
